03:30Z","body":"2.5.1 is a small bug fix release for \"Root Volume Dirty\" error appearing in some cases as well as introducing more clarity.\r\n\r\n----------\r\n\r\n- Fix \"Root Volume Dirty\" appearing after unpatching.\r\n- Reword \"Root Volume Dirty\" to be clearer for users.\r\n\r\n----------\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n## Full Changelog\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>2.5.1 Changelog (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\n- Fix \"Root Volume Dirty\" appearing after unpatching if seal remains broken, for example when an update is pending.\r\n  - Thanks @crystall1nedev \r\n \r\n- Reword \"Root Volume Dirty\" to be clearer for users about what it means.\r\n  - Thanks @crystall1nedev \r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n## Asset Information\r\n\r\n* **OpenCore-Patcher.pkg**:\r\n  * Visual GUI-based app installer\r\n  * Recommended for all users\r\n* OpenCore-Patcher-Uninstaller.pkg:\r\n  * Uninstalls OpenCore-Patcher.app and additional utilities\r\n  * Does not revert any patches installed\r\n* AutoPkg-Assets.pkg:\r\n  * Additional resources used by OpenCore-Patcher\r\n  * Automatically pulled when needed, don't download","is_prerelease":false},"readme":true,"readme_zh":false,"news":[],"stale":false,"snapshot_at":"2026-11-14T08:50:43Z","history_start":"2026-09-06"}